  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Community Engagement and Policing (CEP) and Integrated Border Management (IBM) in Cabo Delgado, Mozambique, and Mtwara, United Republic of Tanzania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the project is to improve community safety and strengthen borders, contributing to peace and stability in Mozambique and United Republic of Tanzania, through the following outcomes. Enhance capacity of Communities and Law Enforcement in Community Engagement and Policing practices in Mozambique and United Republic of Tanzania. Law enforcement has increased capacity in Intelligence Led Policing. The Mozambican National Criminal Investigation Service (SERNIC) has increased capacity in Investigative Policing. Improved cross-border cooperation and capacity between Tanzanian and Mozambican border agencies.</narrative>
  </description>
